WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.871
Welcome to Module 3: Agent Design Patterns.

2
00:00:03.871 --> 00:00:09.280
Patterns are reusable ways to arrange model calls, tools, and checks.

3
00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:21.170
You will learn the difference between workflows and agents, explore eight design patterns with their strengths and limitations, and practice choosing the simplest pattern that solves a task.

4
00:00:22.570 --> 00:00:34.107
The patterns range from a basic responder to sequential, routing, and parallel workflows, then tool calling, evaluator-optimizer loops, plan-and-execute, and multi-agent collaboration.

5
00:00:34.107 --> 00:00:37.430
Each one has a playable diagram and a Python example.

6
00:00:38.830 --> 00:00:45.290
The key takeaway: start with the simplest pattern that works, and add autonomy only when it clearly helps.
